  "decisive_argument": {
    "primitive_integer": "n=floor(L)+1 and n+1 both lie strictly inside (L,U) when U-L>2. One is not divisible by 3. The three residue cases provide explicit integers p,q with iq-3p=1, also for negative endpoints.",
    "height": "dw<1/3 gives R>3W. The interval (d(R-3W),d(R-3a0)) has length 3T/(1+T)>2 since T>=6. Choose its determinant-one integer i and set a=(R-i/d)/3, b=W-a, t=a/b. Interval membership gives a0<a<W and b>0; a0<a gives T<t. The ratio identities follow from a+b=W and bt=a. Height gaps are 3W>0 and R-3W>0, and the total range is i/d+3a=R.",
    "auxiliaries": "Expansion proves tent_slice_length. Dividing the assumed tent bound by R>0 proves compressed_tent_inside_simplex."
  },
